  "notes": "Last-entry drift attacks truncated source-table loops. All malformed source dictionary rows must be refused by type/shape before subscripting. Source fault harness may disable autoloads only in its owned clone. Revision 3 adds two size-preserving 'rename-key' faults (last key removed, its unchanged integer value reinserted under key+\"_renamed\") for Catalog.BUILDING_STATE and Catalog.ROOM_TYPE only. Both faults leave dictionary size and the retained value's type untouched, so they pass every preceding size/type check and are the only witnesses in this plan that a real key is absent from the has()/membership branch of _source_state_refusal and _source_room_type_refusal, closing the F1 coverage gap noted in the independent source-review follow-up. The ROOM_TYPE rename-key case reuses the existing isolated_room owned-clone shim (an equal-valued literal '7' standing in for Catalog.ROOM_TYPE[\"CORRIDOR\"]) for the same compile-fold reason as the missing/last-id-type room faults, since rename-key also removes the last (CORRIDOR) key; BUILDING_STATE needs no such shim because no production alias names its last key. No other dictionary in this plan carries a rename-key case.",
  "revision": 3,
  "disposition": "Independent source review M2 adds dictionary shape/type witnesses (revision 2, 75 cases/675 assertions, retained here unchanged). Revision 3 appends exactly the two rename-key membership-witness cases identified as F1 in the follow-up review, bringing the total to 77 cases / 693 assertions with the bypass-kill total unchanged at 10, since no new bypass expression was introduced. Missing/type/rename-key ROOM_TYPE counterfactuals preserve only the integer CORRIDOR alias in owned cold clones; production unchanged."
}
